cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LunarLeaf-CFD, please cite it as below."
title: "LunarLeaf-CFD: a validated in-browser CFD model of gravity-dependent gas-exchange boundary layers around Arabidopsis"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based lattice-Boltzmann model that solves incompressible flow,
  multi-species (CO2/O2/H2O) advection-diffusion and Boussinesq buoyancy under an
  adjustable gravity vector, validated against four numerical benchmarks and
  anchored to measured Arabidopsis gas exchange. Quantifies how reduced gravity
  thickens the leaf gas-exchange boundary layer across leaf, rosette and canopy
  scales; the forced airflow needed to counteract it; the three ISS growth systems
  (BRIC/CARA/VEGGIE) as boundary conditions; and CO2-limited photosynthesis to
  link transport to carbon gain.
type: software
